Because we're moving on to episode two.
因为我们要进入第二集了。

00:35:13.360 --> 00:35:22.119
I would just say that one thing that struck me watching the pilot was the sense memory of the challenge of having to have Robin meet the rest of the gang.
我只想说，看试播集时触动我的一点是，那种必须让罗宾与其他人相遇的挑战所带来的直观记忆。

00:35:22.119 --> 00:35:25.760
Robin, Kobe Smolder's, only has scenes with Josh in the pilot.
罗宾（寇碧·史莫德斯饰）在试播集中只有和乔什的对手戏。

00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.207
never interacts with anybody else.
她从来没有跟其他人互动过。

00:35:27.207 --> 00:35:38.530
And I remember that feeling at the end of the pilot, like, we better have a good episode, too, that shows how she kind of works her way into this group and be friends with this group because that's a whole other sale we have to make of, like, she's the fifth banana.
我记得在试播集结尾时那种感觉：我们最好在第二集拍个好点的剧情，展现她是如何融入这个群体并和大家成为朋友的，因为这是我们要推销的另一个大点：她算老几。

00:35:38.530 --> 00:35:41.679
She's, you know, she's the, she's the fifth part of this five-part puzzle.
她，你知道的，她，她是这个五人拼图中的第五块。

00:35:41.679 --> 00:35:46.239
And we had to sort of integrate her and show how everybody else kind of fell in love with her, too.
我们得把她融合进来，并展示其他人是如何也开始喜欢上她的。

00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:48.885
And I, I had that feeling in my body.
我当时身体里真切地感受到了那种压力。

00:35:48.885 --> 00:35:53.563
It's sort of re-experienced that, like, we got to somehow thread the needle on out.
重新体验到了那种感觉，就像我们必须在这一点上找到平衡。

00:35:53.563 --> 00:35:54.916
We got to make the sale.
我们得把这个设定卖给观众。

00:35:54.916 --> 00:36:04.498
Like, I remember feeling that way When we had to write episode two and three and that we're sort of like showing her becoming part of that group and yeah It was just fun.
就像我记得当我们不得不写第二集和第三集时那种感觉，我们要展现她如何成为那个群体的一部分，是的，这真的很有趣。

00:36:04.498 --> 00:36:11.037
Remember that challenge and we'll rewatch and talk about if we if we did it I think we did I think we pulled it off.
记住那个挑战，我们接下来会重温并讨论我们是否做到了，我觉得我们做到了，我觉得我们成功了。

00:36:11.037 --> 00:36:26.199
I have two things one is if you watch the pilot of how I met your mother the DNA for the entire show is in the pilot Yeah, like absolutely the entire kind of structure and essence and and surprise switcheroo kind of thing that they did so well, it's all, it's in there.
我有两件事，第一件是如果你看了《老爸老妈浪漫史》的试播集，整部剧的DNA在试播集里就已经具备了。是的，整部剧的结构、精髓以及那种大反转的把戏，他们玩得那么溜的东西，全都在里面了。

00:36:26.199 --> 00:36:27.960
It's like the raggoo sauce or whatever.
就像那个拉古酱或者别的什么一样。

00:36:27.960 --> 00:36:29.280
It's like it's in there.
就像它就在那里面。

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:32.320
What people understand that, you can cut that if they don't.
大家能懂就行，如果不懂的话可以剪掉。

00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:37.119
The other thing I wanted to say, this is just a funny thing that my wife said this morning.
我另外想说的一件事，这只是我太太今天早上说的一个趣事。

00:36:37.119 --> 00:36:50.429
She was like, she knew someone who had, who lived on the upper west side and he had a dog named Teddy and everyone called him the dog Teddy West side.
她说她认识一个人，住在上西区，他有一只狗叫泰迪，大家都叫这只狗“上西区泰迪”。

00:36:50.429 --> 00:36:56.469
And I love, as one of Ted's, he had so many nicknames, Teddy West sides a great nickname, I thought, but it was also self-proclaimed, right?
我觉得，作为泰迪的众多外号之一，“上西区泰迪”真是一个很棒的外号，但这也是他自封的对吧？

00:36:56.469 --> 00:36:57.869
He called himself Teddy West side.
他自称是“上西区泰迪”。

00:36:57.869 --> 00:37:00.110
Yeah, I think he was trying to get everyone else on board.
对，我觉得他当时是想让大家都这么叫。

00:37:00.110 --> 00:37:01.269
They weren't on board.
但大家并不买账。

00:37:01.269 --> 00:37:03.429
Yeah, but she said, so where'd they live?
对，但她就说，那他们住哪儿？

00:37:03.429 --> 00:37:05.949
And I said, they lives on the upper west side, right?
我说，他们住在上西区啊，对吧？

00:37:05.949 --> 00:37:06.789
Yeah.
对。

00:37:06.789 --> 00:37:07.630
Yeah.
对。

00:37:07.630 --> 00:37:10.389
And she said, but Robin lives in Brooklyn.
然后她说，但罗宾住在布鲁克林啊。

00:37:10.389 --> 00:37:19.351
And I said, yeah, she said, because Robin's cool, because we, like, Jordan, she grew up in Manhattan, but she lives in Brooklyn and she just can't stand going into Manhattan.
我说，对啊，她说，因为罗宾很酷，因为我们……就像乔丹一样，她在曼哈顿长大，但她住在布鲁克林，而且她就是受不了去曼哈顿。

00:37:19.351 --> 00:37:20.330
She loves Brooklyn.
她超爱布鲁克林。

00:37:20.330 --> 00:37:25.789
But she said, how was she hanging out on this bar on the upper west side so much if she lived in Brooklyn?
但她说，如果她住在布鲁克林，怎么会经常在上西区的这家酒吧鬼混呢？

00:37:25.789 --> 00:37:26.789
Yeah.
对啊。

00:37:26.789 --> 00:37:28.055
She was terrible.
这太离谱了。

00:37:28.055 --> 00:37:31.183
Here's what I, here's what I rationalized.
我是这么……我是这么合理解释的。

00:37:31.183 --> 00:37:33.789
I think her TV station is close by.
我觉得她的电视台就在附近。

00:37:33.789 --> 00:37:34.289
Yeah.
对。

00:37:34.289 --> 00:37:37.266
Let's say that TV is in mid, TV stations in Midtown somewhere.
比方说电视台在 中城 的某个地方。

00:37:37.266 --> 00:37:38.369
So she's like, why not?
所以她就会想，为什么不呢？

00:37:38.110 --> 00:37:45.550
Or even in like the West 60s, like where the West 60s, like that sort of like CBS building, like West 50s, 60s, that whole thing.
甚至就在西60年代那边，就像西60年代那样，比如哥斯比大楼那种地方，西50年代、60年代，大概就是那一带。

00:37:45.550 --> 00:37:49.429
So then she just pops up a couple of like 10 or 15 blocks and hangs out with her friend.
所以她只要往上走个十街区或十五街区，就能跟朋友一起玩了。

00:37:49.429 --> 00:37:54.710
But also, she's out so late and she has to get up at like 3.30 in the morning to do the early.
不过话说回来，她常常玩到那么晚，然后还得在凌晨3点半左右起床去播早间新闻。

00:37:54.710 --> 00:37:55.989
Just a day, like an hour and a half.
路上只要花个一个半小时吧。

00:37:55.989 --> 00:37:58.429
These are the kind of threads we'll be pulling, that'll be.
这就是我们接下来要探讨的那些细枝末节……

